        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' season teetered on a knife's edge after a brutal 11-0 collapse in Seattle, erasing any momentum from their previous 2-0 shutout win. <strong>The Blue Jays fell to the Mariners 11-0</strong>, a disaster that left them with just one hit and three homers allowed, as Randy Arozarena's grand slam capped a five-run second inning. Now sitting at 42-47 and 11.5 games behind in the AL East, the team's L1 streak underscores a fragile trajectory. Dylan Cease, who set a franchise record with 137 strikeouts in 16 starts, remains the story - dominant in the opener, yet the bullpen imploded in the finale. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. turned down an All-Star invite, signaling a team rethinking its priorities. <strong>Tonight at 5:00 PM ET, the Blue Jays face the Mariners again in a desperate bid to avoid a three-game sweep and reclaim respectability.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
