  "morning_brief": {
    "article": {
      "title": "McKenna Choves Number 92",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Leafs are locking in their future as rookie Gavin McKenna confirms he will wear No. 92, swapping his old 72 to respect veteran goalie Sergei Bobrovsky. This heavy investment signals the team is ready for the next two years of development. Meanwhile, the Jays lost 11-0 to the Mariners last night and face them again today at 5:00 PM ET on Sportsnet. With a 42-47 record and Vladimir Guerrero Jr. declining an All-Star invite, the Blue Jays are looking toward the second half of the season.",
        "The Raptors officially signed Jaden Bradley to a two-way contract, a key move as they prepare to reveal future playoff pieces in the upcoming Summer League. Forward to the Commanders, who are gearing up for training camp with their first game against the Eagles on Sunday, September 13, in 70 days. The team is also focused on the grudge match against the 49ers in Week 6, even as Brandon Aiyuk's path to joining the squad appears to close."
      ]
